speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, pursuant to Standing Order 106, I present a petition on behalf of 4,000-odd people of Canada's Haitian community. Your petitioners humbly request:
That the regime of General Namphy in Haiti be denounced because it is made up of former Duvalier supporters, some of whom are now on trial;
That the Canadian Parliament firmly denounce the so-called democratic approach of this regime since it took over;
That Canadian assistance, earmarked mostly for salaries paid to Canadian volunteers and for project administration expenditures, be suspended until such time as the interim electoral council, whose members have been dismissed by General Namphy, has been reinstated; and
That the Prime Minister urge the United Nations to launch an inquiry into the repeated breaches against human and democratic rights which were witnessed on November 29 and the following days and which are still going on.
The petition of the Haitian people will continue to circulate and gather public support until the disappearance of the Haiti dictatorship and the end of the massacre of these people.
